#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
lil-bench — Built-in Local-Inference-Lab (llm-inference-bench v0.7.9) Runner & Card Generator for Flux Engine.

Supports:
  1. Presets replicating the exact Flux Engine evaluation suites:
     - lil-bench matrix      : All-context prefill + decode matrix (0,8k,16k,32k,64k,128k) at C=1 (or custom --concurrency)
     - lil-bench concurrency : Multi-stream concurrency sweep (default C=1,2,4,8 across 0,8k,32k with --show-capacity-limited-values)
     - lil-bench estonia     : Estonia 136.6K long-context needle-in-a-haystack & coherent synthesis test (--test-profile estonia)
     - lil-bench prefill     : Dedicated long-context prefill sweep (8k,16k,32k,64k,128k)
     - lil-bench coding      : Coding peak generation throughput benchmark (--coding-peak, 5 runs x 2000 tokens)
     - lil-bench accuracy    : Accuracy suite (gsm8k, mmlu-pro, gpqa-diamond; gpqa-diamond skipped in 'all' when HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 unless locally cached)
     - lil-bench suite       : Full unified evaluation (matrix + coding + concurrency + estonia + visual & markdown cards)
     - lil-bench card        : Generate dark-mode SVG/PNG benchmark card + Markdown MODEL_CARD.md from any lil-bench JSON output(s)
  2. Direct pass-through of any raw llm_decode_bench.py flags (e.g. `lil-bench --test-profile estonia --concurrency 1,2,4`).
  3. Privacy-First defaults & opt-in/opt-out controls (default: FLUX_OPT_OUT=all):
     - FLUX_OPT_OUT=all|telemetry|host|logs|none (default: all)
     - --opt-out-telemetry / --no-upload (0 outbound calls; all runs are 100% air-gapped local)
     - --opt-out-host-info (enabled by default; redacts host/GPU/fabric diagnostics & server URL from outputs & cards)
     - --opt-out-prompt-logs (enabled by default; redacts prompt/completion text from JSON artifacts)
     - --include-host-info / FLUX_INCLUDE_HOST_INFO=1 (opt-in to retain raw host/GPU diagnostics)
     - --include-prompt-logs / FLUX_INCLUDE_PROMPT_LOGS=1 (opt-in to retain raw prompt/completion text)
"""

